\c 34  
\d By David; when he pretended to be insane before Abimelech, who drove him away, and he departed.  
\q1
\v 1 \f + \fr 34:1 \ft Psalm 34 is an acrostic poem, with each verse starting with a letter of the alphabet (ordered from Alef to Tav).\f*\w I|strong="H1980"\w* \w will|strong="H6440"\w* bless \w Yahweh|strong="H3068"\w* \w at|strong="H1732"\w* \w all|strong="H6440"\w* \w times|strong="H6440"\w*.  
